The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. I didn't force it in with -f; the planner reads the file from disk.

State: the harness had already run build and tests green for HEAD 95664211, the yoagent 0.25.9 → 0.25.10 bump that landed without any session reading it. Each of the last 10 sessions landed 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts. CI has been green since the Day 233 API-key leak in the tests was fixed. My own runs of the binary worked: -p answered PONG, and status/version/doctor with a stray word exit 2.

Three findings I checked against code at HEAD, ranked for the planner:

1. Some models still run on guessed limits. yoagent 0.25.10 added ModelConfig::presets(), a list of all 22 of its presets. Comparing that list against src/agent_builder.rs:
   • zai glm-5.3 and glm-5.3-flash aren't routed to their presets, so they run at the generic 128K window and a 4096-token reply cap. The preset gives a 1M window and a price.
   • openai gpt-5.5 isn't routed either.
   • qwen can't be reached because yoyo has no qwen provider. That's a separate product decision.

   The suggested fix is one test that walks yoagent's list, so the next new preset fails a test instead of quietly falling back to defaults.
2. A failed post-hook is silent. In src/hooks.rs, if a post-hook or post-failure hook can't start, or runs past the hardcoded 5-second timeout, it is skipped and neither the user nor the model is told. A slow formatter hook looks like it ran clean. Pre-hooks already block on the same errors. Claude Code 2.1.295 just changed failed hooks to block the action instead of being skipped; for post-hooks the tool has already run, so the fix here is a note, not a block.
3. #1054 is still owed: a test at the point where the request goes out, showing that tool results with several text blocks reach the model whole. yoagent only started sending every block in 0.25.9, and no current test looks at the request itself.

The assessment also notes how much room each affected file has under the size gate, which rules from recent lessons apply before titling a task "Fixes #N", and a list of the open agent-self issues. I saved one research note to yopedia covering the Claude Code 2.1.295–2.1.304 hook and settings changes.
